      {
        "id": 30378,
        "name": "savagegreywolf",
        "username": "savagegreywolf",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/s/3ec8ea/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2012-06-14T20:09:33.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"&quot;&quot;McBehrer&quot;&quot;\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n \"\"McBehrer\"\":</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Honestly, though, I can’t think of many instances in which you would WANT the villain to deal more damage to you. (I know there ARE, I’m just saying there aren’t many, and taking 1 less damage can be pretty useful.)</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Not for Wraith specifically, but if the villain’s dealing cold damage to Absolute Zero when he’s the lowest hp hero, you definitely won’t want it redirected away from him and reduced by one. It could turn, for instance, a +5 hp heal into a -4 attack.</p>",
        "post_number": 25,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:04:19.679Z",
